commit 1e80f253313dea164349fef17eac4c4a4fc73b7c
Author: buremba <emrekabakci@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 29 14:29:21 2026 +0000

    fix(agent-worker): stop pinning pi's agentDir under TMPDIR

    The worker's spawn env pins TMPDIR to /workspace/.tmp (assembleBaseEnv),
    so os.tmpdir() resolved there for every worker — including embedded runs
    on a developer or CI host, where /workspace does not exist and cannot be
    created. mkdir'ing the pinned agentDir therefore failed session boot with
    "EACCES: permission denied, mkdir '/workspace'" (sdk-e2e).

    Pin agentDir to a fixed non-existent path and never create it: with all
    discovery flags off pi only existsSync-probes it, so a missing directory
    is the strongest form of empty. It also drops the env dependency, which
    was pointing the "Lobu-owned" dir inside the workspace volume this module
    exists to keep out of resource resolution.

    Co-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>

